WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.025
Two external clocks bear on the
schedule, and they're easy to conflate.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:09.094
FedRAMP's Consolidated Rules
for 2026, announced on June 25,

3
00:00:09.094 --> 00:00:13.025
2026, govern how cloud
services are certified.

4
00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:17.425
They become mandatory for
everyone on January 1, 2027,

5
00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:24.225
and FedRAMP stops accepting new Rev5
certification applications on June 11, 2027.

6
00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:27.125
None of that certifies
the agency's own estate.

7
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:32.279
FedRAMP is explicit that each agency still
authorizes its own federal information

8
00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:37.213
systems, and should never create a standalone
authorization for a cloud service.

9
00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:42.762
What the 2027 date changes is the evidence
your providers publish and you inherit.

10
00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:48.380
The deadlines that bind the agency
directly come from OMB and CISA:

11
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.790
M-26-14's logging plan
and maturity levels,

12
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:59.713
and BOD 25-01's secure configuration
baselines for in-scope Microsoft 365 tenants.

13
00:00:59.713 --> 00:01:01.762
The estate has its own dates too.

14
00:01:01.762 --> 00:01:06.713
Windows 10 reached end of
support on October 14, 2025.

15
00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:14.646
Extended security updates for Windows Server
2012 and 2012 R2 ended on October 13,

16
00:01:14.646 --> 00:01:21.413
2026, and Windows Server 2016 reaches
end of support on January 12, 2027.

17
00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:23.712
Mainframes have a place in the sequence.

18
00:01:23.712 --> 00:01:26.995
Token-based access joins
the access workstream late,

19
00:01:26.995 --> 00:01:32.440
discrete read-mostly transactions first,
and M-22-09 notes that mainframes

20
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:37.288
may need other zero trust mechanisms
where endpoint detection tools don't fit.

21
00:01:37.288 --> 00:01:42.226
So the sponsor and the CIO sequence
the program against the agency's own

22
00:01:42.226 --> 00:01:47.810
deadlines and end-of-support dates, starting
now, not against FedRAMP's 2027 date.
